<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paithan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pratishthana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paithan is a town on the Godavari river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. As ancient Pratishthana it was one of the main cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, named in early Buddhist texts and known to Greek and Roman traders as Paithana. It served as a capital of the Satavahana dynasty and remains a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> weaving, famous for its Paithani saris.</p></div>
